1
00:00:04,304 --> 00:00:08,831
Whiskers and Luna's World. Episode five. Rivers and Lakes!

2
00:00:16,024 --> 00:00:19,433
One rainy morning, the rain went pitter patter.

3
00:00:19,633 --> 00:00:23,662
Rain, rain, go away. Where does all this rain go, anyway?

4
00:00:23,862 --> 00:00:27,929
On an adventure! Rain runs into rivers, and rivers run to the sea.

5
00:00:31,357 --> 00:00:33,814
Let's follow one little raindrop, all the way!

6
00:00:34,014 --> 00:00:35,400
Hold on to the cushion!

7
00:00:44,745 --> 00:00:46,964
Up into space they flew!

8
00:00:53,619 --> 00:00:56,313
Look! The blue lines are rivers. They're everywhere!

9
00:00:59,741 --> 00:01:02,856
This is the Nile, in Africa. It's very, very long!

10
00:01:07,360 --> 00:01:12,208
And this is the Amazon, in South America. The biggest river, with the most water!

11
00:01:16,174 --> 00:01:19,034
The most water? That's a lot of bath time.

12
00:01:21,386 --> 00:01:24,857
Our raindrop's journey starts up in the mountains. To the Alps!

13
00:01:37,430 --> 00:01:41,458
High in the snowy Alps, a little cloud was full of rain.

14
00:01:45,424 --> 00:01:47,624
Wheee! Hello! I'm Drip, a raindrop!

15
00:01:47,824 --> 00:01:49,582
Hello, Drip! Where are you going?

16
00:01:49,782 --> 00:01:53,307
Downhill! Look, the sun is melting the snow. More drops are coming!

17
00:01:57,811 --> 00:02:02,177
Melting snow, like on Mount Everest! Tiny streams run down the mountain.

18
00:02:07,219 --> 00:02:10,170
And when the streams join together, they make a river!

19
00:02:13,598 --> 00:02:15,195
Come on! Jump in!

20
00:02:23,464 --> 00:02:24,707
Wheee! Make way!

21
00:02:24,907 --> 00:02:27,880
Hi! I'm Ollie the otter. This river is my playground!

22
00:02:28,080 --> 00:02:30,741
Why does the river keep going down, down, down?

23
00:02:30,941 --> 00:02:34,531
Rivers always flow downhill, from the high mountains to the low sea.

24
00:02:39,572 --> 00:02:42,908
Wait! My fish snack is up there! Paddle back up!

25
00:02:50,102 --> 00:02:53,860
Ha ha! You can't paddle up a river, Whiskers. Water flows downhill!

26
00:02:54,060 --> 00:02:58,318
I knew that. I went backwards on purpose. It's called relaxing.

27
00:03:08,739 --> 00:03:12,112
Then the river flowed into a big, calm lake.

28
00:03:12,312 --> 00:03:15,590
A lake is a big pool of water, with land all around it.

29
00:03:20,093 --> 00:03:23,776
Last time I drank the sea, it was salty. Bleh!

30
00:03:27,742 --> 00:03:29,688
Hey! It's not salty at all!

31
00:03:29,888 --> 00:03:34,121
River and lake water is fresh, not salty. Lots of animals drink it.

32
00:03:38,625 --> 00:03:41,154
The river flows on. Next stop, the sea!

33
00:03:49,423 --> 00:03:52,639
At last, the river reached the big, salty sea.

34
00:03:52,839 --> 00:03:55,068
I made it! All the way to the sea!

35
00:03:55,268 --> 00:03:57,336
Is this the end of your journey, Drip?

36
00:03:57,536 --> 00:04:00,228
Oh! The warm sun is lifting me up, up, up!

37
00:04:05,270 --> 00:04:10,068
The sun warms the water. It rises as invisible vapour, and makes clouds!

38
00:04:12,958 --> 00:04:16,044
And then I fall as rain again, back on the mountains!

39
00:04:24,851 --> 00:04:27,860
That's the water cycle. Water goes round and round!

40
00:04:31,287 --> 00:04:33,434
Bye, Drip! See you next time it rains!

41
00:04:39,014 --> 00:04:43,417
Remember! One. Rivers flow downhill, all the way to the sea.

42
00:04:46,038 --> 00:04:49,591
Two. River and lake water is fresh, not salty.

43
00:04:52,212 --> 00:04:56,123
Three. Water goes round and round, in the water cycle.

44
00:05:02,241 --> 00:05:05,725
Quiz time! Does a river flow uphill, or downhill?

45
00:05:08,614 --> 00:05:10,305
Downhill! Well done!

46
00:05:12,657 --> 00:05:15,665
Next. Is lake water salty, or fresh?

47
00:05:18,555 --> 00:05:20,543
Fresh! Not salty at all.

48
00:05:27,198 --> 00:05:30,954
And with a twinkle, they were home. The rain had stopped.

49
00:05:31,154 --> 00:05:34,117
Look! A raindrop on the window! Is that you, Drip?

50
00:05:37,007 --> 00:05:40,375
Round and round, like me on my cushion. Goodnight.

51
00:05:43,803 --> 00:05:47,807
Next time, deserts, where it hardly ever rains! Goodnight!

